## The last FAIL is a KLayout bug in our own fork

I root-caused it, and it is not what §7 of my findings first said — I corrected that in §15. Same deck expression, same GDS, one token changed, positive control in the script:

```
                          deep   flat
ctl_vias (positive ctl)     2      2
enclosing_less_edges        5      4      <- delta is ONE edge: the via's TOP
m2.5 (full chain)           1      0
```

That via's top enclosure is 0.280 µm against a 0.085 requirement. `deep` calls it short. The same engine also contradicts itself: inside deep, `via2.not_inside(m3.sized(-0.065))` is empty while `m3.enclosing(via2,0.065)` returns 2.

